{"complete":true,"school_name":"Drexel University","town_name":"Philadelphia","template_id":"college-blocks-off-campus","title":"10 Blocks Off Campus, One Reason Each","description":"Ten nearby corridors and micro-districts, each paired with one practical, directly sourced reason to go.","icon":"location_city","cards":[{"subject_id":"market-30th","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Market Street at 30th Street","title":"Start at the Rail Gateway","subtitle":"For regional and intercity connections","notes":"Walk east on Market Street when you need the campus-side approach to 30th Street Station; use marked crossings and the signed station entrance.","short_summary":"A transportation-focused block at University City’s eastern edge.","evidence_claim":"The 30th Street district provides access to William H. Gray III 30th Street Station and is planned as a gateway with river and park connections.","source_url":"https://www.phila.gov/media/20190517161458/Philadelphia-30th-Street-Station-District-Plan-2016.pdf","source_title":"Philadelphia 30th Street Station District Plan","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2016-06-01","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":39.95578,"longitude":-75.18182,"maps_url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=39.95578&mlon=-75.18182#map=17/39.95578/-75.18182","access_notes":"Active transportation district; follow station rules and use designated crossings and entrances.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lancaster-west-campus","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Lancaster Avenue west of campus","title":"Follow the Athletics Approach","subtitle":"For the route toward Vidas","notes":"Trace the university’s published walking approach along Lancaster and Powelton avenues when heading toward the Vidas Athletic Complex.","short_summary":"A westbound corridor linking the main campus orbit with Drexel athletics.","evidence_claim":"Drexel directs pedestrians toward the Vidas Athletic Complex via Lancaster Avenue and Powelton Avenue.","source_url":"https://drexel.edu/university-recreation/reccenter/fitness-floors/facilities/vidas-athletic-complex","source_title":"Vidas Athletic Complex","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":39.9612,"longitude":-75.2003,"maps_url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=39.9612&mlon=-75.2003#map=16/39.9612/-75.2003","access_notes":"The cited directions establish the route, not present sidewalk conditions or travel time.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"baltimore-40th-51st","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Baltimore Avenue, 40th–51st streets","title":"Catch the Dollar Stroll Corridor","subtitle":"For a recurring neighborhood event","notes":"Check the event date before traveling southwest, then use the organizer’s current map to see which corridor vendors are participating.","short_summary":"A long commercial stretch used for the seasonal Baltimore Avenue Dollar Stroll.","evidence_claim":"University City District identifies Baltimore Avenue from 40th to 51st streets as the commercial corridor for its recurring Dollar Stroll.","source_url":"https://www.universitycity.org/stroll/","source_title":"The Baltimore Avenue Dollar Stroll","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":39.9478,"longitude":-75.213,"maps_url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=39.9478&mlon=-75.213#map=15/39.9478/-75.213","access_notes":"The event is seasonal; participation, dates, and individual offers can change.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"schuylkill-trail-market-chestnut","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Schuylkill River Trail access near Market and Chestnut streets","title":"Join the River Trail","subtitle":"For a mapped cycling connection","notes":"Use the city bicycle map to locate the bridge approaches, and follow its instruction to walk your bicycle on the access ramp.","short_summary":"The nearest mapped bridge approaches into the riverfront trail network.","evidence_claim":"Philadelphia’s bicycle map marks Schuylkill River Trail access from the Market and Chestnut Street bridges near University City.","source_url":"https://www.phila.gov/media/20220520145523/Bike-Map-0520-Spanish.pdf","source_title":"Philadelphia Bicycle Map","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2022-05-20","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":39.9549,"longitude":-75.1802,"maps_url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=39.9549&mlon=-75.1802#map=17/39.9549/-75.1802","access_notes":"The map instructs cyclists to walk bicycles on the bridge access ramp; check separately for closures.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"schuylkill-yards","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Schuylkill Yards","title":"Walk the Public-Art District","subtitle":"For murals and outdoor installations","notes":"Enter the district east of campus and use its experience guide to connect Mural Row, the Highline Park sculpture, and other outdoor works.","short_summary":"A campus-adjacent development district with a documented public-art network.","evidence_claim":"Schuylkill Yards documents a district public-art collection that includes Mural Row, a sculpture at Highline Park, and a mural by David Guinn.","source_url":"https://schuylkillyards.com/experience","source_title":"Experience | Schuylkill Yards","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor works and public spaces may be affected by construction or scheduled events.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ucity-square","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"uCity Square","title":"See the Mixed-Use Science District","subtitle":"For its combination of spaces","notes":"Walk west along Market Street to examine how laboratories and offices sit alongside housing, retail, community uses, and green space.","short_summary":"A nearby mixed-use district organized around science and community space.","evidence_claim":"uCity Square describes its district as containing laboratory, clinical, office, retail, residential, community, and green spaces.","source_url":"https://ucitysquare.com/about/","source_title":"About - uCity Square","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Public outdoor circulation does not imply access to private laboratories, offices, or residences.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"chestnut-34th-45th","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Chestnut Street, 34th–45th streets","title":"Use the Completed Protected Lane","subtitle":"For an eastbound bicycle corridor","notes":"Choose this stretch for an eastbound ride, stay within the parking-protected lane, and watch signals and turning movements at intersections.","short_summary":"A completed parking-protected bicycle segment running through University City.","evidence_claim":"Philadelphia lists the Chestnut Street parking-protected bicycle lane from 33rd to 45th streets as completed.","source_url":"https://www.phila.gov/programs/complete-streets/projects/","source_title":"Complete Streets Projects","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Street infrastructure remains subject to maintenance, construction, and temporary traffic controls.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"40th-street-corridor","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"40th Street corridor","title":"Browse a Multi-Block Retail Spine","subtitle":"For varied storefronts between transit stops","notes":"Walk the blocks between the Market–Frankford Line and trolley portal to survey the corridor’s mix of shops, books, services, and food.","short_summary":"A compact commercial spine bracketed by rapid-transit and trolley access.","evidence_claim":"University City District describes the 40th Street corridor as several commercial blocks between an elevated-train stop and a trolley station, with varied shops and dining.","source_url":"https://www.universitycity.org/press/a-look-at-the-old-timers-on-university-citys-vibrant-40th-street-corridor/","source_title":"A Look at the Old-Timers on University City's Vibrant 40th Street Corridor","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Individual storefront access and operating hours vary; consult each destination directly.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"woodland-va-42nd","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Woodland Avenue, VA Driveway–42nd Street","title":"Read a Corridor in Transition","subtitle":"For an active Complete Streets project","notes":"Review the city project page before visiting, then look for the planned bikeway, crossing, landscaping, lighting, and signal improvements.","short_summary":"A southwest University City corridor undergoing a phased multimodal redesign.","evidence_claim":"Philadelphia’s Woodland Avenue project includes a raised two-way bikeway, new signals and crosswalks, trees, landscaping, and street lighting between the VA driveway and 42nd Street.","source_url":"https://www.phila.gov/programs/complete-streets/projects/woodland-42nd-va/","source_title":"Woodland Avenue Complete Streets Project (VA Driveway to 42nd Street)","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The project is phased and remains in progress; current conditions may differ from the final design.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"walnut-33rd-63rd","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Walnut Street, 33rd–63rd streets","title":"Take the Westbound Bike Counterpart","subtitle":"For a separated cross-city route","notes":"Use Walnut for the westbound leg of a bike trip, remaining alert to posted controls at intersections and any unfinished or repaired segments.","short_summary":"A westbound separated bicycle corridor paired with Chestnut Street’s eastbound lane.","evidence_claim":"Philadelphia identifies the Walnut Street separated bicycle lane from 33rd to 63rd streets as a westbound counterpart to the eastbound Chestnut Street lane.","source_url":"https://www.phila.gov/2024-05-03-city-celebrates-bicycle-safety-month-by-launching-visual-recap-of-2023-bicycle-network-changes-and-announcing-multiple-events/","source_title":"City Celebrates Bicycle Safety Month by Launching Visual Recap of 2023 Bicycle Network Changes","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2024-05-03","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Follow current signs, signals, construction controls, and ordinary street-use rules.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}
